id: pm-extapps-vendor-zod
title: Track upstream ext-apps bundled Zod refresh before adopting its runtime bundles
description: Latest upstream ext-apps2.0.3 embeds Zod4.3.5 in app-with-deps and react-with-deps. A workspace override updates normal dependency imports but cannot rewrite these unused bundles. pm-cli uses only ext-apps/server types and excludes the package from its runtime dependency manifest and published artifact. Track upstream bundle refresh before any future runtime adoption; do not describe dual-feed lockfile success as proof that every vendor byte is patched.
type: Task
status: open
priority: 3
tags[4]: changelog-exclude,dependencies,security,upstream
created_at: "2026-10-23T23:41:18.091Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T00:11:36.875Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: Verify a future upstream release replaces the embedded affected parser in both bundles; preserve the current type-only and artifact-exclusion boundary until that evidence exists; exercise bounded constrained-collection controls before runtime adoption
parent: pm-zod466
risk: low
confidence: 95
expected_result: Future ext-apps runtime adoption requires a verified upstream bundle refresh and constrained-collection controls; current type-only and distribution-exclusion safeguards remain explicit.
